[4c] LOCALIZING THE SURVIVING OBLIGATION (G0-MAX) TO A SINGLE PROFILE CONDITION
     At a UNIT_DOWN state B = A - e_p + e_q (value w lowered, value u raised, w >= u+2),
     max(B) < max(A) IFF the LOWERED entry is the UNIQUE maximum of A.  So (G0-MAX) is
     exactly: the lowered entry is never A's unique maximum.  Measured on P1's g=0 states.
     And by Theorem GAP1 the lowered entry enters at sorted position d+1 of the PARENT,
     so the danger profile is  s^A_1 = ... = s^A_{d+1} > s^A_{d+2}  (a band of exactly
     d+1 copies straight below the pivot).  Both are counted.
     g=0 joint states over P1+P2                       : 1242  (of which non-EQ: 65)
     multiplicity of max(A) at the non-EQ g=0 states   : {2: 49, 3: 16}
     ... where the LOWERED entry IS A's maximum        : 65
     ... where it is A's UNIQUE maximum (the only way (G0-MAX) can fail) : 0
     gap-1 parents carrying the danger cut profile     : 100
     ... (i0 position, outcome) for those parents       : {('i0>d+1', 'EQ'): 100}
     ... and for the i0>d+1 ones, which GAP1 branch     : {'c=u+1(EQ)': 100}
   CONTROL: non-EQ g=0 states exist to be measured                        hits=65       OK
     ==> the lowered entry IS the maximum at every one of these states; (G0-MAX)
         survives ONLY because that maximum always has multiplicity >= 2.
